      "number": 6,
      "title": "Add pull request intake for StatArena data contributions",
      "body": "## What this adds\n\n- A public Contribute data page with two routes: Simulated DGP and Real-data problem. Each route has a Markdown template and a filled JASA example with a DAG, estimand and reproducibility details.\n- One proposal per GitHub pull request, a PR checklist, and a reviewer guide. Private evaluation or restricted materials are handled separately with a maintainer.\n- An automated structural check for new submissions and scoped CODEOWNERS for review routing. The fork check reads the proposed Markdown from GitHub using the trusted base revision. The rollout PR runs the validator's self-tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exercised the homepage and both template links in Chromium at desktop and mobile widths.\n- Ran 10 validator unit tests. Both completed examples pass, while the unfilled templates and invalid fixtures are rejected.\n- Ran the R snippets for both examples using the public source material and checked the reported outputs.\n- Matched the existing site regression expectations to the current homepage and IV baseline.\n\nPublic Pages deployment follows maintainer review and merge.",
