      "number": 9,
      "title": "datasubmission test",
      "body": "This PR adds a simulation proposal for estimating pointwise CATE when treatment effects are strongly localized despite a simple marginal outcome regression. Opposite-signed Gaussian bumps in the treatment-arm means create heterogeneous effects that disappear when the arms are averaged.\n\nThe mechanism comes from Section 5.2 of Rolling and Yang (2014), *Model selection for estimating treatment effects*, **JRSS-B**, 76(4), 749–769. Public sources: [[paper DOI](https://doi.org/10.1111/rssb.12043)](https://doi.org/10.1111/rssb.12043) and [[publisher article](https://academic.oup.com/jrsssb/article/76/4/749/7076033)](https://academic.oup.com/jrsssb/article/76/4/749/7076033). Selecting a fixed CATE query and implementing the collection interface are documented adaptations.\n\nMethods receive the baseline effect modifier `U`, randomized treatment `A`, continuous outcome `Y` and the same query metadata.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    U[\"Pretreatment effect modifier U\"] --> Y[\"Outcome Y\"]\n    A[\"Randomized treatment A\"] --> Y\n```\n\nIdentification assumes independent individuals, consistency, no interference, randomized assignment and positivity. The target is the conditional treatment-versus-control mean difference at the declared query.\n\nThe complete generator, exact settings, selected query, seeds, analytical reference and independent numerical checks are available for agreed private review. Local generation, reproducibility and truth checks have passed. The proposed method comparison has not been run; scientific review and evaluation inclusion remain pending.",
      "state": "open",
      "draft": false,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Statsinference/statsinference.github.io/pull/9",
